251
00:13:46.535 --> 00:13:49.079
I promise you, I'm better at my job
than I am at kickboxing.

252
00:13:49.997 --> 00:13:51.707
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

253
00:13:57.504 --> 00:13:58.629
<i>Great news.</i>

254
00:13:58.630 --> 00:14:01.174
- <i>Today is Half-Price Wednesday...</i>
- You're about to go to size 4S, huh?

255
00:14:01.175 --> 00:14:03.302
Are you so big now, huh? How big is Maxie?

256
00:14:05.888 --> 00:14:06.888
So big.

257
00:14:06.889 --> 00:14:08.348
Look at the big muscles.

258
00:14:11.935 --> 00:14:13.060
Okay, hold on.

259
00:14:13.061 --> 00:14:17.024
We're gonna get this for Mama.
And that. And that.

260
00:14:17.900 --> 00:14:19.276
You wanna get ice cream?

261
00:14:19.818 --> 00:14:21.570
Yeah, I'm gonna get you ice cream.

262
00:14:25.157 --> 00:14:26.283
Yeah?

263
00:14:29.328 --> 00:14:30.953
Yeah. There it is.

264
00:14:30.954 --> 00:14:32.038
You want this one?

265
00:14:32.039 --> 00:14:33.624
I'll get you french fries.

266
00:14:42.007 --> 00:14:43.007
Oh, shit.

267
00:14:45.761 --> 00:14:47.429
I'm so sorry about this, pal.

268
00:14:49.515 --> 00:14:50.641
Really?

269
00:14:55.521 --> 00:14:56.646
Hey, asshole.

270
00:14:56.647 --> 00:14:58.524
At least let me put my kid down.

271
00:15:10.160 --> 00:15:11.370
Oh, shit.

272
00:15:15.415 --> 00:15:17.208
- Daniel.
- I'm so sorry, Mrs. Overmeyer.

273
00:15:17.209 --> 00:15:18.335
Uh-oh.

274
00:15:19.920 --> 00:15:21.295
Oh, my God!

275
00:15:21.296 --> 00:15:22.297
Hey!

276
00:15:37.062 --> 00:15:38.939
I told you to let me put my kid down!

277
00:15:49.867 --> 00:15:51.158
I got 'em.

278
00:15:51.159 --> 00:15:53.620
<i>Cleaning team to aisle three, please.</i>

279
00:15:56.498 --> 00:15:57.498
Sorry about the mess.

280
00:15:57.499 --> 00:15:59.918
Thank you for shopping
at Fresh, Fresh, Fresh.

281
00:16:10.637 --> 00:16:11.805
Hold on.

282
00:16:16.476 --> 00:16:17.895
Hey, Beau.

283
00:16:19.146 --> 00:16:21.565
- Hey, Dan.
- Have a good one.

284
00:16:22.316 --> 00:16:23.483
All right.

285
00:16:41.960 --> 00:16:43.795
Shit. The passports are out of date.

286
00:16:52.596 --> 00:16:54.681
From here on in,
Daddy's paying in cash, Maxie.

287
00:16:56.683 --> 00:16:57.808
<i>Hello?</i>

288
00:16:57.809 --> 00:16:59.685
Hey, don't hang up.

289
00:16:59.686 --> 00:17:01.771
How are you still alive?

290
00:17:01.772 --> 00:17:03.482
Yeah, it's nice to hear your voice too.

291
00:17:03.982 --> 00:17:07.069
Look, I need new identities.
I'm burned. Full packets.

292
00:17:07.986 --> 00:17:09.779
Me, my wife, and three kids.

293
00:17:09.780 --> 00:17:11.905
Three? How did that happen?

294
00:17:11.906 --> 00:17:14.075
Do I really need to explain the birds
and the bees right now, Augie,

295
00:17:14.076 --> 00:17:15.327
or can we talk business?

296
00:17:16.453 --> 00:17:17.745
Oh, God.

297
00:17:17.746 --> 00:17:19.498
You've got some nerve calling me.

298
00:17:20.082 --> 00:17:22.666
McCaffrey scorched the earth
looking for you.

299
00:17:22.667 --> 00:17:24.418
Yep. Looks like he's found me.

300
00:17:24.419 --> 00:17:25.670
- <i>How?</i>
- I don't know.

301
00:17:25.671 --> 00:17:27.046
Social media, I guess.

302
00:17:27.047 --> 00:17:28.214
<i>You idiot.</i>

303
00:17:29.550 --> 00:17:31.467
I had to leave my life behind.

304
00:17:31.468 --> 00:17:36.014
Now I'm stuck in Tempe, Arizona, making
fake IDs for entitled college pricks.

305
00:17:37.015 --> 00:17:40.226
- Should I go?
- Oh, no. You can stay.

306
00:17:40.227 --> 00:17:43.104
But given you're trying to look
like you're not in college,

307
00:17:43.105 --> 00:17:44.398
maybe try losing the hoodie?

308
00:17:46.108 --> 00:17:47.828
Look, I'll pay you
a half a million in cash.

309
00:17:48.443 --> 00:17:50.803
<i>And you get Doris a condo
in one of those retirement places.</i>

310
00:17:51.238 --> 00:17:53.739
You know, the ones with the golf carts,
the wine and cheese happy hour,

311
00:17:53.740 --> 00:17:54.949
mah-jongg at six o'clock?

312
00:17:54.950 --> 00:17:56.409
Leave my mom out of this.

313
00:17:56.410 --> 00:17:58.703
- <i>She'll love it.</i>
- I can sell you out for twice that.

314
00:17:58.704 --> 00:18:00.372
Well, you haven't in 18 years.

315
00:18:00.873 --> 00:18:02.875
Meet me in Vegas in three days.

316
00:18:05.961 --> 00:18:07.795
I'll give you a time and a place
once I'm on the road.

317
00:18:07.796 --> 00:18:09.463
Vegas? Why Vegas?

318
00:18:09.464 --> 00:18:12.425
I can't tell my wife I'm taking her
on vacation to Tempe, Arizona.

319
00:18:12.426 --> 00:18:13.343
Vegas, I can sell.

320
00:18:13.344 --> 00:18:15.595
You haven't told them? Are you mental?

321
00:18:15.596 --> 00:18:17.805
What, do you think it's that easy?
What am I meant to do?

322
00:18:17.806 --> 00:18:19.932
Sit them down and tell them
the whole story over French toast?

323
00:18:19.933 --> 00:18:22.518
<i>Oh, hey, kids. You know what?
Pass the maple syrup. By the way,</i>

324
00:18:22.519 --> 00:18:24.562
your dad was a government assassin.

325
00:18:24.563 --> 00:18:27.083
I'll tell them when I'm on the road
and safe. Three days, Augie.

326
00:18:32.863 --> 00:18:33.989
Chess club.

327
00:18:40.579 --> 00:18:41.580
All right, come on.

328
00:18:52.216 --> 00:18:53.717
Where's Nina?

329
00:18:54.968 --> 00:18:56.886
Nina's not the editor anymore. She quit.

330
00:18:56.887 --> 00:18:58.305
What? When?

331
00:18:58.972 --> 00:19:00.056
Three months ago.

332
00:19:00.057 --> 00:19:01.600
So, where is she now?

333
00:19:02.518 --> 00:19:03.726
I don't know.

334
00:19:03.727 --> 00:19:04.894
All right, look.

335
00:19:04.895 --> 00:19:07.021
I'll give you 50 bucks
for your best guess of where Nina is.

336
00:19:07.022 --> 00:19:09.565
I'm a journalist. I don't give people up.

337
00:19:09.566 --> 00:19:10.900
100.

338
00:19:10.901 --> 00:19:12.276
Try under the bleachers.

339
00:19:12.277 --> 00:19:13.737
That's what I thought.

340
00:19:20.452 --> 00:19:24.163
I wrote my college essay on how
universities propagate systemic racism,

341
00:19:24.164 --> 00:19:25.373
and my mom shot it down.

342
00:19:25.374 --> 00:19:26.541
I was like, "Hello,

343
00:19:26.542 --> 00:19:27.750
that's how change happens."

344
00:19:27.751 --> 00:19:29.991
And she goes, "No, that's how
community college happens."

345
00:19:30.379 --> 00:19:31.463
Nina.

346
00:19:32.297 --> 00:19:33.798
Dad, what are you doing here?

347
00:19:33.799 --> 00:19:35.967
This is a safe space.
He can't just come in here.

348
00:19:35.968 --> 00:19:37.052
Your dad's hot.

349
00:19:38.011 --> 00:19:39.762
Okay, Kelly. That's gross.

350
00:19:39.763 --> 00:19:41.264
You're meant to be
in an editorial meeting.

351
00:19:41.265 --> 00:19:43.266
Yeah, I am. I was.

352
00:19:43.267 --> 00:19:45.226
- I...
- You quit three months ago.

353
00:19:45.227 --> 00:19:47.478
How could you do that?
You worked so hard to become editor.

354
00:19:47.479 --> 00:19:49.730
- You don't even read my stuff.
- Of course I do.

355
00:19:49.731 --> 00:19:51.148
- I always do.
- Yeah. Bullshit.

356
00:19:51.149 --> 00:19:53.234
You know what? I don't have time for this.
Where's the chess club?

357
00:19:53.235 --> 00:19:55.319
- We need to find your brother.
- Can't you tell me what's going on?

358
00:19:55.320 --> 00:19:57.321
Nothing. I have a surprise
for the family, okay?

359
00:19:57.322 --> 00:19:59.949
- What's the surprise?
- Where is the chess club?

360
00:19:59.950 --> 00:20:02.326
It's in the math building.

361
00:20:02.327 --> 00:20:03.620
Thank you, Kelly.

362
00:20:05.122 --> 00:20:07.040
- Dad, wait.
- What now?

363
00:20:08.125 --> 00:20:09.334
He's not there.

364
00:20:17.426 --> 00:20:18.593
Stay in the car.

365
00:20:18.594 --> 00:20:20.595
Oh, no. Forget it. I am not missing this.

366
00:20:20.596 --> 00:20:22.514
- Missing what?
- Nothing.

367
00:20:23.724 --> 00:20:24.933
Go, go, go, go, go.

368
00:20:28.353 --> 00:20:30.104
- Shit.
- Are you Samir?

369
00:20:30.105 --> 00:20:31.940
- Yeah.
- I'm Kyle's dad. Is he here?

370
00:20:38.822 --> 00:20:40.239
What happened to chess club?

371
00:20:40.240 --> 00:20:42.033
It was canceled today.

372
00:20:42.034 --> 00:20:44.578
- Right, Samir?
- You don't pay me to lie.

373
00:20:45.120 --> 00:20:46.955
- You pay him?
- No, I...

374
00:20:49.208 --> 00:20:50.584
You don't need to... It's...

375
00:20:55.088 --> 00:20:56.255
- I can explain.
- Get in the car.

376
00:20:56.256 --> 00:20:58.550
- I...
- Get in the car.

377
00:20:59.134 --> 00:21:00.134
Let's go now.

378
00:21:02.888 --> 00:21:03.888
Traitor.

379
00:21:13.607 --> 00:21:16.192
- So, what's the big surprise?
- We're going on a trip.

380
00:21:16.193 --> 00:21:18.069
I actually have plans this weekend, so I...

381
00:21:18.070 --> 00:21:19.430
You're very grounded, both of you.

382
00:21:29.540 --> 00:21:31.040
<i>Look, we're going up there
to get your mom.</i>

383
00:21:31.041 --> 00:21:33.334
You two are gonna show her
nothing but excitement for this trip,

384
00:21:33.335 --> 00:21:35.086
or I'm gonna tell her
that you've been lying to us,

385
00:21:35.087 --> 00:21:36.713
and you know how that's gonna go down.

386
00:21:37.339 --> 00:21:38.631
Where are we even going?

387
00:21:38.632 --> 00:21:39.716
<i>Vegas?</i>

388
00:21:40.300 --> 00:21:42.760
- We're going to Las Vegas today?
- Well, you said you wanted...

389
00:21:42.761 --> 00:21:44.095
- Now?
- To be more spontaneous.

390
00:21:44.096 --> 00:21:46.097
I heard you. And Jorge said
I could take a few days off.

391
00:21:46.098 --> 00:21:47.890
Is Jorge the one that does...

392
00:21:47.891 --> 00:21:50.935
- hydromassages on Tuesdays?
- No, Mrs. Kessler. Jorge is Dan's boss.

393
00:21:50.936 --> 00:21:54.814
- Is Dan giving me a hydromassage?
- No, Mrs. Kessler.

394
00:21:54.815 --> 00:21:56.065
There's no massages today.

395
00:21:56.066 --> 00:21:58.192
No. The kids have a long weekend,
and they're pumped. Right, guys?

396
00:21:58.193 --> 00:22:00.654
Guys, tell your mom
how pumped you are for this trip.

397
00:22:01.530 --> 00:22:03.532
- Yes!
- So pumped.

398
00:22:04.032 --> 00:22:06.450
Dan, we can't just up and go to Vegas.

399
00:22:06.451 --> 00:22:08.327
I mean... And why Vegas?

400
00:22:08.328 --> 00:22:12.248
I know it's not Europe,
but there's a Venice and an Eiffel Tower.

401
00:22:12.249 --> 00:22:14.834
You know what? I bet you
we can get last-minute Adele tickets.

402
00:22:14.835 --> 00:22:16.544
- You love Adele.
- You love Adele.

403
00:22:16.545 --> 00:22:18.296
Of course I love Adele.
Who doesn't love Adele?

404
00:22:18.297 --> 00:22:20.173
- I love Adele.
- Everybody loves Adele.

405
00:22:20.174 --> 00:22:22.008
She's got the voice of a freaking angel.

406
00:22:22.009 --> 00:22:24.468
Come on, Jess. What is holding us back?

407
00:22:24.469 --> 00:22:27.638
Who are you? I mean,
I don't even recognize you.

408
00:22:27.639 --> 00:22:29.808
Well, you're gonna love him.
He's crazy in bed.

409
00:22:31.268 --> 00:22:32.810
Are you sure it's not Tuesday?

410
00:22:32.811 --> 00:22:35.813
You deserve a break. And I think this
could be really good for us as a family.

411
00:22:35.814 --> 00:22:37.565
And we're driving there?

412
00:22:37.566 --> 00:22:39.766
Well, nothing brings
a family together like a road trip.

413
00:22:41.320 --> 00:22:43.446
But we gotta go now.
Before the traffic gets bad.

414
00:22:43.447 --> 00:22:46.073
And Mrs. Kessler, I'm so sorry.
You keep working on those deltoids, okay?

415
00:22:46.074 --> 00:22:48.034
- Thanks, Jorge.
- What about our stuff?

416
00:22:48.035 --> 00:22:50.411
- I mean, I need to pack, the baby. It's...
- Oh, no.

417
00:22:50.412 --> 00:22:52.538
I got all the basics packed already.
Yeah. When we get there,

418
00:22:52.539 --> 00:22:55.124
we're gonna use the money that we
saved on flights to go all <i>Pretty Woman</i>

419
00:22:55.125 --> 00:22:56.542
in those fancy hotel boutiques...

420
00:22:56.543 --> 00:22:58.336
- that smell like leather and patchouli.
- Stop.

421
00:22:58.337 --> 00:23:00.672
And guess who's got no budget?
You get whatever you want.

422
00:23:02.257 --> 00:23:05.009
Okay. This is totally crazy.

423
00:23:05.010 --> 00:23:06.594
- Dan, this is crazy.
- I know. It's crazy.

424
00:23:06.595 --> 00:23:07.887
- Oh, my God.
- We're gonna get crazy.

425
00:23:07.888 --> 00:23:09.431
We're going to Vegas!

426
00:23:10.599 --> 00:23:11.807
Do we have snacks?

427
00:23:11.808 --> 00:23:13.184
Let's just get out there on the road,

428
00:23:13.185 --> 00:23:14.853
and then we can make a stop and...

429
00:23:19.816 --> 00:23:22.902
I think I'm gonna take a shortcut.
Save us a little bit of time.

430
00:23:22.903 --> 00:23:24.321
What?

431
00:23:29.451 --> 00:23:30.494
Go, go, go!

432
00:23:31.495 --> 00:23:33.829
- Shit.
- It's a shortcut. You never take Elmwood?

433
00:23:33.830 --> 00:23:34.830
Shit.

434
00:23:43.465 --> 00:23:44.675
All right. We're off.

435
00:23:51.849 --> 00:23:53.100
Hey, Maxie.

436
00:23:53.684 --> 00:23:54.935
- First road trip.
- Yeah.

437
00:23:56.019 --> 00:23:57.854
Max, you excited?

438
00:23:57.855 --> 00:24:01.023
Five hours on a plane,
or 33 hours in a car?

439
00:24:01.024 --> 00:24:02.192
I choose 33 hours.

440
00:24:03.026 --> 00:24:04.236
Da!

441
00:24:12.035 --> 00:24:13.828
Honey, you remembered my boots!

442
00:24:13.829 --> 00:24:15.705
- Yeah.
- Baby!

443
00:24:15.706 --> 00:24:16.874
I can't believe that.

444
00:24:23.213 --> 00:24:25.590
- Oh, my God. Jesus. Dad.
- Jesus.

445
00:24:25.591 --> 00:24:27.383
- Easy there, lead-foot.
- Sorry about that.

446
00:24:27.384 --> 00:24:29.584
Think a squirrel or something
jumped out in front of me.

447
00:24:31.555 --> 00:24:33.181
Oh, my God.

448
00:24:33.182 --> 00:24:36.100
- Where on earth are you taking us?
- What? Oh, no. This is a shortcut, honey.

449
00:24:36.101 --> 00:24:37.394
You never take it?

450
00:24:39.146 --> 00:24:40.146
Shit.

451
00:24:43.525 --> 00:24:44.735
He's tracking us.

452
00:24:45.319 --> 00:24:46.402
Oh, nothing.

453
00:24:46.403 --> 00:24:47.529
Nothing, honey.

454
00:24:56.788 --> 00:25:00.334
You know what? Actually, I gotta stop
and check something at work real quick.

455
00:25:10.177 --> 00:25:13.179
- Is that Hal?
- Yeah. He's got a new mustache.

456
00:25:13.180 --> 00:25:15.260
- You work with that guy?
- It will just be a second.

457
00:25:20.604 --> 00:25:22.324
I think there's a service area
to the right.

458
00:25:32.241 --> 00:25:35.786
All right. If you guys just give me
a second, I'll be right there.

459
00:25:41.667 --> 00:25:43.585
- Dad, what the hell?
- Language, Nina.

460
00:25:44.711 --> 00:25:46.045
Dan, what the hell?

461
00:25:46.046 --> 00:25:47.630
Oh, well, we're driving 2,000 miles.

462
00:25:47.631 --> 00:25:49.550
We've gotta change the oil,
check the coolant,

463
00:25:50.801 --> 00:25:52.051
pop a little extra air in the tires.

464
00:25:52.052 --> 00:25:54.846
I'd hate to be halfway across the desert
and wish we'd checked that coolant, right?

465
00:25:54.847 --> 00:25:56.974
Can we not be in the car for it?

466
00:26:01.520 --> 00:26:03.480
Okay, he's stopped.
He's right ahead of us.

467
00:26:25.377 --> 00:26:26.503
He should be here.

468
00:26:34.970 --> 00:26:37.138
Hey, guys.
Just hang in there for a minute.

469
00:26:37.139 --> 00:26:38.223
Dan?

470
00:26:39.183 --> 00:26:40.766
Mom, when we're in Vegas,

471
00:26:40.767 --> 00:26:43.436
- can I go to HyperX?
- No, you're not going to a strip club.

472
00:26:43.437 --> 00:26:45.021
- It's not a strip club.
- Why are you laughing?

473
00:26:45.022 --> 00:26:46.230
You're not gambling, Nina.

474
00:26:46.231 --> 00:26:47.773
- Do you have a fake ID?
- I'm not being... No.

475
00:26:47.774 --> 00:26:49.108
Dan!

476
00:26:49.109 --> 00:26:51.736
Hey, Hal. Nice wheels.

477
00:26:51.737 --> 00:26:53.070
- She just come in?
- Yeah.

478
00:26:53.071 --> 00:26:54.822
I was thinking about
opening her up a little bit.

479
00:26:54.823 --> 00:26:58.117
Oh, man. I tell you what.
She wants to go fast.

480
00:26:58.118 --> 00:26:59.285
Cars are like chicks, man.

481
00:26:59.286 --> 00:27:01.621
- Yes! Right.
- Get her on the freeway.

482
00:27:01.622 --> 00:27:03.749
You open her up.
And you get a ticket, it's on me.

483
00:27:09.338 --> 00:27:11.632
I got him. He's on the move.
He's heading west.

484
00:27:16.553 --> 00:27:17.637
Hey, guys.

485
00:27:17.638 --> 00:27:18.804
- Yes?
- We're ready.

486
00:27:18.805 --> 00:27:21.057
Are we going to Vegas,
or are we just gonna live up here?

487
00:27:21.058 --> 00:27:22.601
We're on our way, honey.

488
00:27:50.462 --> 00:27:53.715
- Honey, aren't your feet cold?
- I don't care. I am on vacation.

489
00:27:54.800 --> 00:27:55.800
What are you doing?

490
00:27:55.801 --> 00:27:57.344
I'm posting about our trip.

491
00:27:58.262 --> 00:28:00.555
Look, do we really need to be posting
and tweeting and TikToking?

492
00:28:00.556 --> 00:28:01.931
In my day,
road trips were all about interaction.

493
00:28:01.932 --> 00:28:04.016
No, Dad. Please. I can't deal
with a dad lecture right now.

494
00:28:04.017 --> 00:28:06.602
You literally don't even know how to text,
