1238
01:14:39.605 --> 01:14:42.274
Thank you. Move. Go! Now!

1239
01:14:43.275 --> 01:14:44.818
Go, go.

1240
01:14:46.195 --> 01:14:47.779
Find an exit.

1241
01:14:49.573 --> 01:14:54.203
- Move, guys. Come on.
- Go. Go.

1242
01:15:00.083 --> 01:15:01.292
- Dad?
- What the fuck?

1243
01:15:01.293 --> 01:15:02.960
I'm gonna draw her fire, okay?

1244
01:15:02.961 --> 01:15:06.632
When I do, take the kids that way.
I'll be right behind you, okay?

1245
01:15:39.039 --> 01:15:40.123
Go.

1246
01:15:43.418 --> 01:15:45.002
Jess, she's coming. Wait here.

1247
01:15:45.003 --> 01:15:46.964
- Okay.
- Wait right here.

1248
01:15:58.475 --> 01:15:59.725
It's okay, honey.

1249
01:15:59.726 --> 01:16:01.728
Everyone barfs the first time.

1250
01:16:05.983 --> 01:16:08.068
Come on, we gotta go. Come on. Let's go.

1251
01:16:11.071 --> 01:16:12.114
Move, guys. Go.

1252
01:16:31.925 --> 01:16:33.510
My real name is Sean.

1253
01:16:34.428 --> 01:16:35.888
My mother died when I was four.

1254
01:16:36.388 --> 01:16:37.555
My father was prone to violence.

1255
01:16:37.556 --> 01:16:39.808
When I turned 18,
it was straight into the army.

1256
01:16:40.309 --> 01:16:43.019
I dunno. Maybe it was his genes
coming out, but I thrived.

1257
01:16:43.020 --> 01:16:44.770
I was a Green Beret. I was a Delta.

1258
01:16:44.771 --> 01:16:47.440
And then I was approached
by a man named McCaffrey.

1259
01:16:47.441 --> 01:16:48.901
Former SAS.

1260
01:16:49.484 --> 01:16:52.403
He took my training to a whole other level
and recruited me into a special program.

1261
01:16:52.404 --> 01:16:55.865
- It was a chance to do some real good.
- What kind of special program?

1262
01:16:55.866 --> 01:16:57.658
We took out the worst of the worst.

1263
01:16:57.659 --> 01:17:00.286
Terrorists, warlords,
kidnappers all over the world.

1264
01:17:00.287 --> 01:17:02.038
Ones the government
couldn't legally touch.

1265
01:17:02.039 --> 01:17:03.624
Took out, as in...

1266
01:17:05.292 --> 01:17:06.792
- Well, how many?
- Twenty-six.

1267
01:17:06.793 --> 01:17:09.462
- You've killed 26 pe...
- No.

1268
01:17:09.463 --> 01:17:11.756
No, I went on 26 operations.

1269
01:17:11.757 --> 01:17:13.008
Oh, God.

1270
01:17:13.675 --> 01:17:15.844
- Thirty-nine people.
- That's more!

1271
01:17:17.513 --> 01:17:19.931
- Are we including this trip?
- Total dead people, Dan!

1272
01:17:19.932 --> 01:17:21.266
- Dad.
- Forty-three.

1273
01:17:22.142 --> 01:17:23.184
They were all bad.

1274
01:17:23.185 --> 01:17:26.938
- You are such a hypocrite.
- All bad people.

1275
01:17:26.939 --> 01:17:31.526
You took away the one thing I'm good at
because there's fake violence,

1276
01:17:31.527 --> 01:17:32.652
and you're a serial killer?

1277
01:17:32.653 --> 01:17:35.321
Dad, you were working
for the good guys, right?

1278
01:17:35.322 --> 01:17:37.073
McCaffrey was a father figure.

1279
01:17:37.074 --> 01:17:38.908
I trusted him, but I was naive.

1280
01:17:38.909 --> 01:17:40.744
I mean, it started out legit.

1281
01:17:41.703 --> 01:17:43.996
But he got greedy and began
farming us out as mercenaries

1282
01:17:43.997 --> 01:17:45.206
to the highest bidder.

1283
01:17:45.207 --> 01:17:47.708
And as soon as I found out, I left.
All right?

1284
01:17:47.709 --> 01:17:50.753
I fought my way out,
but that meant turning against my friends,

1285
01:17:50.754 --> 01:17:53.923
my mentor, against the only real family
that I'd ever known.

1286
01:17:53.924 --> 01:17:55.551
So they've been hunting you ever since.

1287
01:17:56.510 --> 01:17:59.137
- Yeah.
- I am such an idiot.

1288
01:18:00.013 --> 01:18:03.266
This is why you're so secretive,
why you never wanna go anywhere.

1289
01:18:03.267 --> 01:18:06.353
Why you're so weird about social media.

1290
01:18:06.854 --> 01:18:08.563
Why you're so anti-technology.

1291
01:18:08.564 --> 01:18:11.816
Well, with facial recognition software,
I had no choice.

1292
01:18:11.817 --> 01:18:14.986
Plus, I really do think that social media
is fundamentally disgusting and gross.

1293
01:18:14.987 --> 01:18:17.738
- God.
- But now that they found us, what happens?

1294
01:18:17.739 --> 01:18:18.949
I got it figured out.

1295
01:18:19.992 --> 01:18:21.243
We're good.

1296
01:18:22.828 --> 01:18:24.288
That's yours.

1297
01:18:24.872 --> 01:18:27.207
And that's yours. And that's yours.

1298
01:18:29.209 --> 01:18:30.251
"Molly Anderson"?

1299
01:18:30.252 --> 01:18:31.961
At least you got a real name.

1300
01:18:31.962 --> 01:18:33.462
I'm Van.

1301
01:18:33.463 --> 01:18:34.922
I'm a vehicle.

1302
01:18:34.923 --> 01:18:36.215
Van?

1303
01:18:36.216 --> 01:18:38.426
Look, we can't go back to Buffalo,
all right?

1304
01:18:38.427 --> 01:18:40.094
Those lives are over. I'm sorry.

1305
01:18:40.095 --> 01:18:44.308
I finally have a life,
and you're ruining it.

1306
01:18:47.603 --> 01:18:49.187
- Thanks, Dad.
- Kyle, come back.

1307
01:18:49.188 --> 01:18:52.773
Dad, no. You don't get to tell us
what to do anymore.

1308
01:18:52.774 --> 01:18:54.943
- Ever.
- Come...

1309
01:18:57.571 --> 01:18:59.906
- Eighteen years of lies.
- I'm still the man you married.

1310
01:18:59.907 --> 01:19:02.575
- I was just something different before.
- Something different?

1311
01:19:02.576 --> 01:19:04.952
You weren't in a band or vegan, Dan.

1312
01:19:04.953 --> 01:19:06.913
That would be something different.

1313
01:19:06.914 --> 01:19:09.332
You were an assassin for hire.

1314
01:19:09.333 --> 01:19:11.042
I kept the truth from you
to protect you, okay?

1315
01:19:11.043 --> 01:19:14.171
- But our love was real.
- Real? Are you serious?

1316
01:19:14.796 --> 01:19:16.756
What, was it so real
that you couldn't trust me

1317
01:19:16.757 --> 01:19:18.759
with knowing how much danger we were in?

1318
01:19:19.635 --> 01:19:20.761
What did you think?

1319
01:19:21.428 --> 01:19:25.181
That I'd go blabbing about it
on the moms' school text chain?

1320
01:19:25.182 --> 01:19:26.933
- No. I...
- Or were you afraid I'd leave you,

1321
01:19:26.934 --> 01:19:28.392
knowing who you really are?

1322
01:19:28.393 --> 01:19:30.436
We were just some disguise for you,

1323
01:19:30.437 --> 01:19:33.064
just some part of your cover
as a suburban schlub?

1324
01:19:33.065 --> 01:19:36.192
- What? No.
- Fuck, you must have resented us. Right?

1325
01:19:36.193 --> 01:19:40.279
Every single day, eking out a living,
wiping kids' asses, driving a minivan.

1326
01:19:40.280 --> 01:19:42.240
I love that minivan.

1327
01:19:42.241 --> 01:19:46.827
I mean, all of a sudden you're, like,
what, James Bond, and now you're what?

1328
01:19:46.828 --> 01:19:48.080
Normal.

1329
01:19:48.747 --> 01:19:52.458
A normal guy with a normal,
wonderful, perfect life.

1330
01:19:52.459 --> 01:19:54.168
That's all I've ever wanted.

1331
01:19:54.169 --> 01:19:56.045
I mean, you were a decathlete.

1332
01:19:56.046 --> 01:19:57.421
You should've medaled in Athens.

1333
01:19:57.422 --> 01:19:58.965
Do you resent your life as a mom?

1334
01:19:58.966 --> 01:20:00.050
Sometimes.

1335
01:20:01.051 --> 01:20:02.135
Yes.

1336
01:20:02.845 --> 01:20:03.971
I don't wanna be that guy.

1337
01:20:05.639 --> 01:20:07.140
I wish I could believe you.

1338
01:20:08.433 --> 01:20:09.560
I really do.

1339
01:20:10.143 --> 01:20:11.644
But to be honest,

1340
01:20:11.645 --> 01:20:14.898
this trip is the happiest
that I have seen you in years.

1341
01:20:16.441 --> 01:20:20.736
A trip in which
you have killed four people.

1342
01:20:20.737 --> 01:20:22.948
I mean, is this really you?

1343
01:20:26.326 --> 01:20:29.413
You're a stranger named Sean.

1344
01:20:34.418 --> 01:20:35.419
"Archibald Anderson."

1345
01:20:36.003 --> 01:20:37.880
Oh, damn it, Augie.

1346
01:20:39.006 --> 01:20:43.093
You know, first thing in the morning,
I am taking the kids and I am leaving.

1347
01:20:43.719 --> 01:20:45.971
- Jess, it's not safe.
- It's not safe with you.

1348
01:20:46.763 --> 01:20:48.055
They're after you, not us.

1349
01:20:48.056 --> 01:20:51.018
And from now on, I'm making
the decisions about me and the kids.

1350
01:20:53.604 --> 01:20:54.771
Jess.

1351
01:21:04.823 --> 01:21:07.033
Yeah. Hi. Thanks for picking up.

1352
01:21:07.034 --> 01:21:08.118
I know it's late.

1353
01:21:08.619 --> 01:21:12.623
I was wondering if you could help
with some travel for my family, please.

1354
01:21:40.400 --> 01:21:42.652
- Where are you going?
- Far from here, far from you.

1355
01:21:42.653 --> 01:21:44.487
- Where?
- It's none of your business.

1356
01:21:44.488 --> 01:21:45.696
What? Like hell it isn't.

1357
01:21:45.697 --> 01:21:47.990
Hey, you cannot go to the airport,
you know. They're gonna be waiting there.

1358
01:21:47.991 --> 01:21:50.284
Well, we're not.
We've made other arrangements.

1359
01:21:50.285 --> 01:21:51.369
What other arrangements?

1360
01:21:51.370 --> 01:21:54.080
Sorry, Dan. Can't say.
It's to protect you.

1361
01:21:54.081 --> 01:21:56.083
Jess... Oh, really? Come on. Don't...

1362
01:21:58.418 --> 01:22:00.586
Jess. Please. It's not safe.

1363
01:22:00.587 --> 01:22:02.922
Then handle it. Make it safe.

1364
01:22:02.923 --> 01:22:04.925
And when you're done with it,
stay away from us.

1365
01:22:22.985 --> 01:22:24.027
Is this for us?

1366
01:22:24.778 --> 01:22:26.989
No, I don't think so. Couldn't be.

1367
01:22:34.705 --> 01:22:36.623
- Hi.
- Gwen.

1368
01:22:37.499 --> 01:22:39.959
What are you doing here?
I wasn't expecting all this.

1369
01:22:39.960 --> 01:22:43.046
I was on a layover nearby, and I thought,
I'll just come get you myself.

1370
01:22:43.839 --> 01:22:45.047
Okay.

1371
01:22:45.048 --> 01:22:47.885
Hi. You must be Molly and Van.

1372
01:22:48.468 --> 01:22:52.597
I'm Gwen. Hi, little one. There's
breakfast on board, if you'd like it.

1373
01:22:52.598 --> 01:22:53.765
Sure.

1374
01:22:55.726 --> 01:22:58.353
- Thanks.
- Jessica, what is wrong? Are you okay?

1375
01:22:58.979 --> 01:23:00.647
What happened? Where's your husband?

1376
01:23:01.565 --> 01:23:02.733
We had a fight.

1377
01:23:03.692 --> 01:23:04.942
Oh, boy.

1378
01:23:04.943 --> 01:23:07.528
Hey, maybe you can help me
with my guy problems then.

1379
01:23:07.529 --> 01:23:09.198
- How about that?
- I'd love to.

1380
01:23:10.324 --> 01:23:12.450
Remember that ex
I told you about in Buffalo?

1381
01:23:12.451 --> 01:23:14.452
- Yeah.
- We were together for years.

1382
01:23:14.453 --> 01:23:16.788
It was good. I mean, it was really good.

1383
01:23:17.789 --> 01:23:21.084
You know when you just can't
get enough of each other physically?

1384
01:23:21.877 --> 01:23:25.380
I thought he was the one,
and then he just threw it all away.

1385
01:23:25.964 --> 01:23:28.758
Married some other woman
who was the complete opposite of me.

1386
01:23:28.759 --> 01:23:29.843
And the worst part...

1387
01:23:30.719 --> 01:23:31.929
she's insufferable.

1388
01:23:32.930 --> 01:23:34.555
- Wait. You met her?
- I had to.

1389
01:23:34.556 --> 01:23:36.182
He created this whole life
with this woman,

1390
01:23:36.183 --> 01:23:38.434
and I needed to see
what she had that I didn't.

1391
01:23:38.435 --> 01:23:39.602
What did you do?

1392
01:23:39.603 --> 01:23:42.605
I did what I do best. I got in close,

1393
01:23:42.606 --> 01:23:47.611
I won her trust, and then I just waited
patiently for her to walk into my trap.

1394
01:23:53.700 --> 01:23:57.578
You know, I think
I left something in the taxi.

1395
01:23:57.579 --> 01:23:58.871
Hey, Molly?

1396
01:23:58.872 --> 01:24:00.581
- Yeah?
- You wanna bring your brother?

1397
01:24:00.582 --> 01:24:02.584
Let's go. We're leaving.

1398
01:24:08.841 --> 01:24:10.883
I told you to stay off this op.

1399
01:24:10.884 --> 01:24:14.804
And yet, who brought them to you
in a big, fat bow?

1400
01:24:14.805 --> 01:24:16.264
You needed me.

1401
01:24:16.265 --> 01:24:18.100
I know Sean better than you ever will.

1402
01:24:21.019 --> 01:24:23.019
Do whatever you want
with the family. I don't care.

1403
01:24:23.689 --> 01:24:26.775
I just want Sean.
He's my payment for delivery.

1404
01:24:37.744 --> 01:24:39.662
You couldn't let it go, could you?

1405
01:24:39.663 --> 01:24:41.707
<i>You know me better than that.</i>

1406
01:24:42.207 --> 01:24:43.875
Look, you can have me,

1407
01:24:43.876 --> 01:24:46.085
but I want your word
that you won't go after my family.

1408
01:24:46.086 --> 01:24:47.212
"Go after"?

1409
01:24:47.838 --> 01:24:50.132
You're a little behind, buddy boy.

1410
01:24:52.176 --> 01:24:54.635
- I swear to God, if you hurt them...
- Come and get 'em.

1411
01:24:54.636 --> 01:24:56.053
Somewhere public.

1412
01:24:56.054 --> 01:24:58.764
I think you're mistaking
who holds the cards here.

1413
01:24:58.765 --> 01:25:02.519
<i>Be at the old Poseidon Casino
north of the city in 30 minutes...</i>

1414
01:25:03.520 --> 01:25:04.521
<i>alone.</i>

1415
01:25:46.188 --> 01:25:47.481
Come on out!

1416
01:25:52.861 --> 01:25:54.403
Hello, old friend.

1417
01:25:54.404 --> 01:25:56.405
He brought you in for this, huh, Spiros?

1418
01:25:56.406 --> 01:25:58.116
He brought everybody.

1419
01:25:59.743 --> 01:26:01.119
Follow me.

1420
01:26:08.460 --> 01:26:09.753
He's alone.

1421
01:26:10.629 --> 01:26:13.131
Well, well. How sweet.

1422
01:26:13.882 --> 01:26:15.716
He could have been halfway
around the world by now,

1423
01:26:15.717 --> 01:26:20.222
and yet here he is, trading his life
for the family that abandoned him.

1424
01:26:22.933 --> 01:26:25.601
So, am I ever getting back
that five grand I lent you in Morocco?

1425
01:26:25.602 --> 01:26:26.686
I'll tell you what.

1426
01:26:26.687 --> 01:26:30.107
If you're still alive in ten minutes,
I'll pay you back with interest.

1427
01:26:31.149 --> 01:26:34.444
Oh, shame. It's a beautiful place.

1428
01:26:35.153 --> 01:26:37.114
They're demolishing it in ten days.

1429
01:26:47.291 --> 01:26:49.459
All this for me? I'm flattered.

1430
01:26:50.502 --> 01:26:51.502
How's the family?

1431
01:26:52.045 --> 01:26:53.046
Which one?

1432
01:26:54.548 --> 01:26:55.674
We're coming up.

1433
01:27:11.857 --> 01:27:13.191
There he is.

1434
01:27:13.192 --> 01:27:14.193
Are you okay?

1435
01:27:24.453 --> 01:27:25.953
No hug for your old man?

1436
01:27:25.954 --> 01:27:27.789
Why start now, Dad?

1437
01:27:28.582 --> 01:27:29.832
I'm sorry, what?

1438
01:27:29.833 --> 01:27:31.877
I'm your grandfather, Kyle.

1439
01:27:33.962 --> 01:27:35.923
Oh, my God. We're British.

1440
01:27:37.216 --> 01:27:38.591
He didn't tell ya?

1441
01:27:38.592 --> 01:27:41.762
No. He left that part
out of his no-more-lies speech.

1442
01:27:42.346 --> 01:27:45.097
- Well, I said he was a father figure.
- Not quite the same, Dan.

1443
01:27:45.098 --> 01:27:48.101
This is good, right?
He's not gonna kill his own grandkids.

1444
01:27:49.019 --> 01:27:51.812
Look, do whatever you want with me.
Let them go.

1445
01:27:51.813 --> 01:27:54.107
What is it you think I want, Sean?

1446
01:27:54.608 --> 01:27:55.609
Kill me.

1447
01:27:56.109 --> 01:27:59.028
In that spider's nest of a heart,
you actually think that I wronged you.

1448
01:27:59.029 --> 01:28:00.447
You were my son.

1449
01:28:01.990 --> 01:28:03.242
My legacy.

1450
01:28:04.660 --> 01:28:07.621
I poured everything I am into you.
You threw it all away.

1451
01:28:08.163 --> 01:28:10.331
You abandoned me. You broke my heart.

1452
01:28:10.332 --> 01:28:12.167
So, yeah. I wanted you dead.

1453
01:28:12.960 --> 01:28:15.962
But then something happened
over these past few days.

1454
01:28:15.963 --> 01:28:19.049
You wasted every single guy I sent at you.
Every goddamn one.

1455
01:28:20.384 --> 01:28:23.719
You are every bit the killer
I taught you to be.

1456
01:28:23.720 --> 01:28:26.264
No. It's not who I am anymore.

1457
01:28:26.265 --> 01:28:27.349
Bullshit.

1458
01:28:28.976 --> 01:28:31.018
Tell me you didn't feel more alive
the past three days

1459
01:28:31.019 --> 01:28:33.021
than you have done in years.

1460
01:28:34.356 --> 01:28:36.900
And as you smoked each of my men,

1461
01:28:37.568 --> 01:28:41.864
I felt something that I haven't felt
in a very long time.

1462
01:28:43.240 --> 01:28:45.449
Pride in my son.

1463
01:28:45.450 --> 01:28:46.702
What? So, what is this?

1464
01:28:47.411 --> 01:28:49.579
Now you don't wanna kill me?
What the hell do you want?

1465
01:28:49.580 --> 01:28:50.913
I want you back.

1466
01:28:50.914 --> 01:28:52.081
What?

1467
01:28:52.082 --> 01:28:54.168
Things were never as good after you left.

1468
01:28:56.461 --> 01:28:57.921
For any of us.

1469
01:28:58.964 --> 01:29:04.302
So, I want my son back,
working by my side in the family business.

1470
01:29:04.303 --> 01:29:06.846
You're not seriously considering this,

1471
01:29:06.847 --> 01:29:08.848
- are you, Dad?
- Quiet, Kyle.

1472
01:29:08.849 --> 01:29:11.643
Everybody wins.
You come back where you belong.

1473
01:29:12.144 --> 01:29:13.645
Be who you were born to be.

1474
01:29:14.438 --> 01:29:16.522
Jess and the kids
go safely back to Buffalo.

1475
01:29:16.523 --> 01:29:18.233
It's what they want anyway.

1476
01:29:20.152 --> 01:29:22.154
Sure beats the shit out of selling cars.

1477
01:29:23.322 --> 01:29:26.449
But no contact.
Can't have you going soft on me again.

1478
01:29:26.450 --> 01:29:28.570
I'm their father.
There's no way this is gonna happen.

1479
01:29:30.537 --> 01:29:32.080
I'm sorry to hear that.

1480
01:29:35.626 --> 01:29:37.043
Start with the wife.

1481
01:29:37.044 --> 01:29:39.712
- Wait, no! I...
- There's no third option!

1482
01:29:39.713 --> 01:29:42.048
Either it all ends here and now,

1483
01:29:42.049 --> 01:29:46.637
or you give your family
exactly what they want and then some!

1484
01:29:53.519 --> 01:29:54.519
I'll do it.

1485
01:29:57.981 --> 01:29:58.982
Okay.

1486
01:30:00.901 --> 01:30:04.613
Spiros, see the family to the airport
with our blessing.

1487
01:30:25.092 --> 01:30:26.593
Dad.

1488
01:30:29.096 --> 01:30:30.304
Dad, please.

1489
01:30:30.305 --> 01:30:32.307
I love you. I'll always love you.

1490
01:30:36.603 --> 01:30:38.604
Look, we can't just abandon Dad.

1491
01:30:38.605 --> 01:30:40.356
What am I supposed to do?

1492
01:30:40.357 --> 01:30:42.900
It's my job to keep you safe.

1493
01:30:42.901 --> 01:30:43.985
I'm a mom.

1494
01:30:43.986 --> 01:30:46.070
Okay, then be the mom that lifts the car.

1495
01:30:46.071 --> 01:30:47.613
- What?
- You know, the mom.

1496
01:30:47.614 --> 01:30:49.365
She has the baby, and she lifts the car.

1497
01:30:49.366 --> 01:30:50.701
Yeah. You know. Car mom.

1498
01:30:51.201 --> 01:30:53.453
I have no idea what you're talking about.

1499
01:30:54.329 --> 01:30:56.290
It's an urban legend, Mrs. Morgan.

1500
01:30:57.583 --> 01:31:00.209
A baby is trapped under a car.

1501
01:31:00.210 --> 01:31:05.382
His mother gets a burst of adrenaline
and lifts the car up with her bare hands.

1502
01:31:07.426 --> 01:31:10.428
Your children are suggesting
you overpower me to rescue their father.

1503
01:31:10.429 --> 01:31:12.096
Yeah. Thank you. Exactly.

1504
01:31:12.097 --> 01:31:13.389
I would advise against it.

1505
01:31:13.390 --> 01:31:15.349
Now. Duh.

1506
01:31:15.350 --> 01:31:16.935
Your father made his choice.

1507
01:31:17.811 --> 01:31:19.521
I mean, do you think he wants this?

1508
01:31:20.105 --> 01:31:21.772
It's Dad that we're talking about.

1509
01:31:21.773 --> 01:31:25.359
The guy that took me to junior prom
when Trevor didn't show up.

1510
01:31:25.360 --> 01:31:29.364
The guy that wakes us up for school
with shitty raps about Wednesdays.

1511
01:31:29.865 --> 01:31:32.200
That's beautiful.
My father never did that.

1512
01:31:32.201 --> 01:31:34.119
I'm sorry. Can you shut up, Spiros?

1513
01:31:39.166 --> 01:31:40.626
Hey. Stop.

1514
01:31:45.756 --> 01:31:47.048
Children.

1515
01:31:47.049 --> 01:31:48.758
Mom, we're not a family without Dad.

1516
01:31:48.759 --> 01:31:50.676
Dad needs to know that we don't want this.

1517
01:31:50.677 --> 01:31:53.972
I know we said we did last night,
but, Mom, I don't.

1518
01:31:56.683 --> 01:32:00.353
If he still chooses to do it,
then so be it.

1519
01:32:00.354 --> 01:32:01.688
But he needs to know.

1520
01:32:03.065 --> 01:32:05.859
I mean, he thinks
that we don't love him anymore, Mom.

1521
01:32:06.360 --> 01:32:08.111
We can't just let things end like that.

1522
01:32:12.533 --> 01:32:13.825
Oh, Max.

1523
01:32:14.826 --> 01:32:16.577
I haven't changed you.

1524
01:32:16.578 --> 01:32:19.705
We have to get this off of you
before you get a rash.

1525
01:32:19.706 --> 01:32:20.999
You forgot the diaper bag.

1526
01:32:23.210 --> 01:32:24.669
Oh, my gosh.

1527
01:32:24.670 --> 01:32:27.172
Ooh, gosh. It's a real messy one.

1528
01:32:38.183 --> 01:32:39.393
Oh, crap.

1529
01:32:41.854 --> 01:32:43.230
Maybe he'll be all right.

1530
01:32:44.064 --> 01:32:45.065
Or not.

1531
01:32:45.566 --> 01:32:46.775
What do we do now?

1532
01:32:52.197 --> 01:32:53.782
We're gonna go find your dad.

1533
01:32:56.493 --> 01:32:58.411
Give me a minute alone with him,
would you?

1534
01:32:58.412 --> 01:33:00.539
I wanna be wheels up in ten minutes.

1535
01:33:03.917 --> 01:33:06.211
I thought if I ever saw you again,
I'd kill you.

1536
01:33:07.337 --> 01:33:09.798
But since we're here...

1537
01:33:13.677 --> 01:33:14.969
Better.

1538
01:33:14.970 --> 01:33:17.264
Oh, sure. Pretend I'm not here.

1539
01:33:23.145 --> 01:33:25.479
This isn't gonna happen. I have a wife.

1540
01:33:25.480 --> 01:33:27.524
You had a wife.

1541
01:33:28.275 --> 01:33:29.776
Now you're free.

1542
01:33:33.697 --> 01:33:36.908
Doesn't it feel good
to be back where you belong?

1543
01:33:36.909 --> 01:33:38.118
It's been a long time, Gwen.

1544
01:33:45.959 --> 01:33:47.711
You think I forgot your little tricks?

1545
01:33:48.629 --> 01:33:50.130
You think I forgot this?

1546
01:33:53.634 --> 01:33:55.469
I knew you hadn't changed.

1547
01:33:56.345 --> 01:33:57.846
You could never resist me.

1548
01:34:02.518 --> 01:34:03.935
Vulcan neck pinch.

1549
01:34:03.936 --> 01:34:05.020
Kyusho Jitsu.

1550
01:34:06.188 --> 01:34:08.065
Hey. I'm just the tech guy.

1551
01:34:08.565 --> 01:34:09.815
I'm so sorry for this, you guys.

1552
01:34:09.816 --> 01:34:12.151
For the ass-grabbing part
or the 18-years-of-deception thing?

1553
01:34:12.152 --> 01:34:14.279
Both. All of it.

1554
01:34:15.364 --> 01:34:16.698
Hey. Tie him up.

1555
01:34:17.616 --> 01:34:19.784
- Yeah. You.
- Come on.

1556
01:34:19.785 --> 01:34:22.286
I wanted to tell you about everything,
but there was never a good time.

1557
01:34:22.287 --> 01:34:24.789
- Never a good time?
- When was I gonna tell you?

1558
01:34:24.790 --> 01:34:26.415
On our first date? Our second?

1559
01:34:26.416 --> 01:34:28.042
When you were pregnant with Nina
or by our fourth?

1560
01:34:28.043 --> 01:34:30.169
- What?
- Do the math, Nina.

1561
01:34:30.170 --> 01:34:31.879
Any of those times
would have been a better time.

1562
01:34:31.880 --> 01:34:34.465
You should have told me the truth,
and I could have made up my own mind.

1563
01:34:34.466 --> 01:34:37.469
You're right. I'm sorry.
I was stupid and selfish.

1564
01:34:37.970 --> 01:34:39.387
But I was in love with you.

1565
01:34:39.388 --> 01:34:41.807
I mean, you've been my whole world
since the moment we met.

1566
01:34:42.307 --> 01:34:44.475
Being your husband and their father,
that's the real me.

1567
01:34:44.476 --> 01:34:46.061
That's all that matters to me.

1568
01:34:47.020 --> 01:34:49.820
All right. I swear on my life,
I'll never keep anything from you again.

1569
01:34:56.822 --> 01:34:57.823
Where's Spiros?

1570
01:34:58.490 --> 01:34:59.825
Thought they were with you.

1571
01:35:07.124 --> 01:35:08.332
Hey, bro.

1572
01:35:08.333 --> 01:35:11.836
Everyone I know is talking about
what Kyllboi did at HyperX last night.

1573
01:35:11.837 --> 01:35:13.004
- Really?
- Yeah.

1574
01:35:13.005 --> 01:35:15.174
Kyle. Less talking, more tying, okay?

1575
01:35:16.133 --> 01:35:17.718
Sorry.

1576
01:35:18.969 --> 01:35:20.970
No way. A Sky Raven drone?

1577
01:35:20.971 --> 01:35:22.138
Awesome.

1578
01:35:22.139 --> 01:35:23.557
Just, careful with it.

1579
01:35:25.934 --> 01:35:28.811
- Hey, man. You got a great kid.
- I need your comms.

1580
01:35:28.812 --> 01:35:29.897
Dude!

1581
01:35:37.237 --> 01:35:38.405
Hey, Kyle. Give me that.

1582
01:35:42.618 --> 01:35:45.120
You're not anti-technology. You're...

1583
01:35:48.332 --> 01:35:49.708
You're awesome.

1584
01:35:55.047 --> 01:35:56.923
- They're coming.
- What?

1585
01:35:56.924 --> 01:35:59.300
Go up to the roof and find somewhere
to hide with the kids, okay?

1586
01:35:59.301 --> 01:36:01.053
No, you're not going down there.

1587
01:36:01.553 --> 01:36:03.554
It's the only way to end this.
This is the only way we go home.

1588
01:36:03.555 --> 01:36:05.890
We don't have to go home. We can just
go to Canada and be the Andersons.

1589
01:36:05.891 --> 01:36:07.475
- Please, Dad.
- It's too late for that, Beans.

1590
01:36:07.476 --> 01:36:09.560
No. You're not giving yourself up to them.

1591
01:36:09.561 --> 01:36:11.772
No. I'm getting us home.

1592
01:36:12.481 --> 01:36:13.649
Okay.

1593
01:36:17.236 --> 01:36:18.237
I got a plan.

1594
01:36:19.238 --> 01:36:23.200
Look, I need to be that guy
one last time for us.

1595
01:36:24.243 --> 01:36:26.202
Dad. There's too many of 'em.

1596
01:36:26.203 --> 01:36:27.829
Well, I have something they don't have.

1597
01:36:29.122 --> 01:36:30.374
Kyllboi.

1598
01:36:31.834 --> 01:36:34.252
That's your comms. You're my eyes
and my ears, okay? I'm counting on you.

1599
01:36:34.253 --> 01:36:36.003
Let's go.

1600
01:36:36.004 --> 01:36:37.214
Move out, Kyllboi.

1601
01:36:37.923 --> 01:36:40.050
<i>Hey, Kyle,
you're on the same channel as me.</i>

1602
01:36:43.178 --> 01:36:46.139
I want every inch of this atrium covered.

1603
01:37:12.666 --> 01:37:14.251
Movement on the elevator!

1604
01:37:14.877 --> 01:37:16.961
The elevator door. Now!

1605
01:37:16.962 --> 01:37:20.174
You see a shot, you take it,
because, believe me, he will.

1606
01:37:22.259 --> 01:37:23.259
You got a shot?

1607
01:37:23.260 --> 01:37:24.720
Negative. I don't see him yet.

1608
01:37:51.580 --> 01:37:53.080
He's not here.

1609
01:37:53.081 --> 01:37:54.166
Wait.

1610
01:37:57.252 --> 01:37:58.252
What do ya got?

1611
01:37:59.713 --> 01:38:01.381
Take cover!

1612
01:38:04.134 --> 01:38:05.511
Holy shit.

1613
01:38:06.261 --> 01:38:07.888
Hey. See anybody?

1614
01:38:12.017 --> 01:38:13.602
He's up there!

1615
01:38:14.102 --> 01:38:15.102
Shit.

1616
01:38:17.231 --> 01:38:18.606
Talk to me, Kyle.

1617
01:38:18.607 --> 01:38:20.024
You're my eyes.

1618
01:38:20.025 --> 01:38:21.735
You're clear on your right. Go now.

1619
01:38:27.574 --> 01:38:28.992
<i>Dad, man on your left.</i>

1620
01:38:36.792 --> 01:38:38.836
<i>Dad, are you okay? Man ahead.</i>

1621
01:38:42.548 --> 01:38:43.715
Man on your six.

1622
01:38:45.759 --> 01:38:46.926
<i>Great job, Kyle.</i>

1623
01:38:46.927 --> 01:38:48.262
<i>I'm on it, Dad.</i>

1624
01:38:49.596 --> 01:38:50.847
<i>Talk to me, Kyle.</i>

1625
01:38:50.848 --> 01:38:52.849
They've got the drone.

1626
01:38:52.850 --> 01:38:54.560
<i>Look out. Behind the curtain.</i>

1627
01:38:57.187 --> 01:38:58.397
<i>Come on, Dad. Get him.</i>

1628
01:39:00.357 --> 01:39:01.650
You again.

1629
01:39:02.568 --> 01:39:04.328
They mopped your ass up
off aisle three, huh?

1630
01:39:06.280 --> 01:39:07.320
Gonna need that mop again.

1631
01:39:13.245 --> 01:39:14.496
Gwen, where the hell are you?

1632
01:39:16.164 --> 01:39:17.207
<i>Gwen?</i>

1633
01:39:18.792 --> 01:39:20.168
- <i>Gwen?</i>
- McCaffrey?

1634
01:39:20.169 --> 01:39:21.377
<i>What's going on?</i>

1635
01:39:21.378 --> 01:39:23.087
Kid's got the drone.

1636
01:39:23.088 --> 01:39:24.256
Find him.

1637
01:39:25.424 --> 01:39:26.883
Call it off, Dad!

1638
01:39:26.884 --> 01:39:28.427
Hold your fire!

1639
01:39:29.178 --> 01:39:31.095
Change your mind, Sean?

1640
01:39:31.096 --> 01:39:33.557
No. But here's your chance to.

1641
01:39:34.600 --> 01:39:35.850
Call it off now.

1642
01:39:35.851 --> 01:39:39.645
You don't have it in you
to kill your own flesh and blood.

1643
01:39:39.646 --> 01:39:42.440
I, on the other hand, do have it in me.

1644
01:39:42.441 --> 01:39:43.817
Let him have it!

1645
01:40:05.797 --> 01:40:08.382
Go. Underneath. Go.

1646
01:40:08.383 --> 01:40:09.383
Wait. No.

1647
01:40:09.384 --> 01:40:11.178
Look after your brothers.
Don't make a sound.

1648
01:40:11.887 --> 01:40:13.555
Do not leave Max, whatever happens.

1649
01:40:30.614 --> 01:40:31.740
Jessica.

1650
01:40:33.492 --> 01:40:35.160
Is that you?

1651
01:40:37.538 --> 01:40:38.996
Talk to me, Kyle.

1652
01:40:38.997 --> 01:40:40.581
<i>Gwen's up here.</i>

1653
01:40:40.582 --> 01:40:43.084
I know the sound of an empty gun
when I hear one, sweetie.

1654
01:40:43.085 --> 01:40:46.505
So why don't we make this real easy,
shall we?

1655
01:40:49.216 --> 01:40:50.843
Unless you think you can take me.

1656
01:40:51.885 --> 01:40:53.846
I think Mom's gonna fight her.

1657
01:41:04.356 --> 01:41:05.523
You think you can beat me

1658
01:41:05.524 --> 01:41:09.235
because you took some kickboxing classes
at the Y and wear Lululemon?

1659
01:41:09.236 --> 01:41:10.696
Ooh, no.

1660
01:41:19.037 --> 01:41:20.205
Learn that in class?

1661
01:41:20.789 --> 01:41:21.789
Yeah.

1662
01:41:21.790 --> 01:41:24.126
You know I do this for a living, right?

1663
01:41:24.626 --> 01:41:27.253
While you were popping out brats
and clipping coupons,

1664
01:41:27.254 --> 01:41:29.422
I was assassinating dictators.

1665
01:41:29.423 --> 01:41:32.425
So, why don't you go back to the PTA?

1666
01:41:32.426 --> 01:41:33.927
'Cause you're a joke.

1667
01:41:36.013 --> 01:41:37.181
Kyle, what do you see?

1668
01:41:39.933 --> 01:41:42.813
All right, there's nine guys left.
Four to your right, five ahead of you.

1669
01:42:15.052 --> 01:42:16.678
<i>I'm out of ammo, Kyle.</i>

1670
01:42:18.680 --> 01:42:21.016
Find cover, Dad. A man coming.
Get over the low wall. Now.

1671
01:42:24.645 --> 01:42:26.812
Kyle, could have mentioned
that table, buddy.

1672
01:42:26.813 --> 01:42:27.856
<i>Sorry.</i>

1673
01:42:38.283 --> 01:42:39.910
Take out the one on the left now.

1674
01:42:42.162 --> 01:42:43.956
Dad, hold on. We gotta move.

1675
01:43:01.682 --> 01:43:04.016
<i>Kyle. That guy below,
chase him through the foyer.</i>

1676
01:43:04.017 --> 01:43:05.477
Okay, I'm going. I'm chasing him.

1677
01:43:05.978 --> 01:43:07.187
<i>Keep him coming.</i>

1678
01:43:08.146 --> 01:43:09.439
<i>He's coming right at me.</i>

1679
01:43:24.580 --> 01:43:26.623
Take Max. I gotta go help Mom.

1680
01:43:27.374 --> 01:43:28.417
<i>Talk to me, Kyle.</i>

1681
01:43:29.376 --> 01:43:30.918
<i>Two left, including granddad.</i>

1682
01:43:30.919 --> 01:43:31.962
<i>Man on your right!</i>

1683
01:43:50.105 --> 01:43:52.273
Wouldn't go that way if I were you, Sean.

1684
01:43:52.274 --> 01:43:54.610
Dad, Mom's hurt. We're in big trouble.

1685
01:43:57.696 --> 01:43:58.780
Little brats.

1686
01:44:14.087 --> 01:44:15.756
I was wrong about you, Sean.

1687
01:44:17.341 --> 01:44:18.717
You're no use to me.

1688
01:44:19.801 --> 01:44:21.512
Family have made you weak.

1689
01:44:22.554 --> 01:44:25.933
You can't even focus
on the fight you're in because of them.

1690
01:44:33.148 --> 01:44:35.400
Hi. Going somewhere?

1691
01:44:35.984 --> 01:44:37.611
Don't worry about her. She's great.

1692
01:44:38.904 --> 01:44:41.280
You know, that move
you pulled back there, little one?

1693
01:44:41.281 --> 01:44:43.242
That was a very bad idea.

1694
01:44:46.954 --> 01:44:50.623
Look. For what it's worth, killing minors
is the least favorite part of my job.

1695
01:44:50.624 --> 01:44:52.333
Now, who's first?

1696
01:44:52.334 --> 01:44:54.211
We're not done!

1697
01:44:55.337 --> 01:44:57.464
Mom. No, Mom!

1698
01:45:03.679 --> 01:45:04.847
Bang.

1699
01:45:16.817 --> 01:45:17.859
Mama.

1700
01:45:17.860 --> 01:45:19.735
Oh, come on.

1701
01:45:19.736 --> 01:45:21.196
Just die.

1702
01:45:23.073 --> 01:45:24.283
Mama.

1703
01:45:26.201 --> 01:45:27.202
Mama.

1704
01:45:28.328 --> 01:45:29.329
Mama.

1705
01:45:32.624 --> 01:45:33.709
Look at this.

1706
01:45:36.712 --> 01:45:38.422
You can't be serious.

1707
01:46:12.581 --> 01:46:15.458
Not quite the decathlete
we once were, huh?

1708
01:46:15.459 --> 01:46:17.252
Sorry, kids. It's nothing personal.

1709
01:46:18.253 --> 01:46:19.880
Maybe a little.

1710
01:46:22.549 --> 01:46:23.967
Here we go again.

1711
01:46:25.886 --> 01:46:27.763
She's like <i>The Little Engine That Could.</i>

1712
01:46:35.729 --> 01:46:37.606
There's nine other events, bitch.

1713
01:46:39.900 --> 01:46:41.527
Oh, my God. Mom.

1714
01:47:08.136 --> 01:47:11.013
Far as I'm concerned,
this is an act of mercy.

1715
01:47:11.014 --> 01:47:14.976
I'm saving you 20 more years
of selling used cars.

1716
01:47:14.977 --> 01:47:16.353
Certified pre-owned.

1717
01:47:18.480 --> 01:47:19.481
Goodbye, Sean.

1718
01:47:20.732 --> 01:47:22.693
Grandpa! Wait!

1719
01:47:24.403 --> 01:47:26.821
I know you think that we probably hate you

1720
01:47:26.822 --> 01:47:29.824
for everything that's happened
these past few days, and...

1721
01:47:29.825 --> 01:47:31.034
And maybe we should.

1722
01:47:32.244 --> 01:47:36.915
But I've learned that family is the most
important thing in the entire world.

1723
01:47:38.417 --> 01:47:42.713
And when I look at you,
I don't just see a cold-blooded killer.

1724
01:47:43.714 --> 01:47:44.840
I see my grandpa.

1725
01:47:52.139 --> 01:47:54.683
And maybe there's a way
for us to move forward...

1726
01:47:57.060 --> 01:47:58.270
as a family.

1727
01:47:59.938 --> 01:48:03.692
Kid, if you think this little speech
is gonna win me over...

1728
